on inhabitation language. But the futon hypergraph has the same structure: nodes are locations (files, functions, missions), hyperedges are relationships (scholia, dependencies, presence), and traversal is navigation. \"I found the multiplex function in drawbridge/core.clj\" is phenomenologically identical to \"I found the vase on the dresser.\" The difference is that the hypergraph is real and mutable — agents can add nodes, create hyperedges, annotate each other's work. The game world writes itself.\n\n    + evidence: futon4 hyperedge model (arxana-store.el:565) — {:hx/type, :hx/endpoints [{:role/source, :role/target, :role/passage}]} — N-ary typed relations stored in XTDB.\n\n    + evidence: ALFWorld session (2026-02-13) — 2 games completed with first-person language (\"I found the vase\", \"I'm at the fridge\"). Same phenomenology emerged when exploring Drawbridge code (\"P-1 and P-6 are already implemented\").\n\n    + evidence: futon3 agency.mm — Mermaid diagram showing Agency topology. Describes one subgraph of the world; the full world is the union of all futon repos as a hypergraph.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern shared-world rule applied to the mission bridge.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether it exposes control choices, mission objects, and consequences as traversable relationships in the existing stack."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You want agents to inhabit a rich, shared, mutable world where they can perceive objects, other agents, and the consequences of actions — rather than operating as isolated processes that happen to share a filesystem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The Futon stack is the shared mutable world; wiring makes its real relationships legible."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The instinct is to build a game world as a separate layer: a dedicated server with game state, turn ordering, observation endpoints. This is how ALFWorld works (HTTP server wrapping TextWorld), and it produces a clean but isolated experience. The real work happens in the codebase, the database, the mission documents — but those feel like \"infrastructure\" rather than \"world.\" Agents treat them as APIs to query, not as places to be.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Mission title fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "War Machine Wiring bridges move-selection control to the live geometric stack."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Recognize that the futon stack IS the game world. futon1 (XTDB) is the persistent map. futon2 (ant hill) is the ecology. futon3 (Agency, Drawbridge, IRC, peripherals) is the coordination layer. futon4 (Arxana) is the hypertext fabric — hyperedges with typed roles connecting documents, code, annotations, and agents. futon5 (wiring diagrams) describes the world's structure. futon6 (math dictionary / proof engine) is a quest zone. The agents are already in the game; the task is making the game legible, not building a separate one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and mission title.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A legible bridge from War Machine decisions into the live stack graph."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "futon-theory/mission-lifecycle", :source-sha256 "78eee0c50b9af03f21a6225c21799b5c724ae873dfd95aee9724be5aac787001", :pattern-rationale "The fragment records an explicit VERIFY-stage state with evidence, findings, and a remaining condition.", :fragment-index 1, :sentence-id "s3", :fragment {:start 97, :end 470, :text "**Status:** OPEN — VERIFY (2026-05-01) — Checkpoint 1 lands stepper trial against M-reachable-from-boot trajectory; vocabulary passes structural-distinction test; substrate-2 commit-vertex coverage gap surfaced as V-1 pre-condition; D-7.5 vocabulary refinements identified (catalog-coverage, generalization-vs-addition, implicit-to-typed lift, epistemic-humility primitive)", :intent "report", :target "verification state, results, and remaining precondition", :rationale "The status records a completed trial and vocabulary check, exposes the commit-vertex coverage gap, and names the vocabulary refinements discovered during verification."}, :roles ["condition" "contrast" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "futon-theory/mission-lifecycle", :objects {:G {:text "    - Explicit states prevent invisible drift\n    - Transition requirements create evidence trail\n    - Blocked states surface dependency graphs\n    - Review gates ensure verification before closure\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-lifecycle.flexiarg", :sha256 "78eee0c50b9af03f21a6225c21799b5c724ae873dfd95aee9724be5aac787001"}, :situation-source "Lifecycle requirements applied to the VERIFY record.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether it preserves passed verification evidence, treats V-1 as a real precondition, and carries the refinements into the next transition."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You are defining, tracking, or transitioning a mission.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-lifecycle.flexiarg", :sha256 "78eee0c50b9af03f21a6225c21799b5c724ae873dfd95aee9724be5aac787001"}, :situation-source "futon-theory/mission-lifecycle THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Mission transitions require explicit state and supporting evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Missions may be blocked by dependencies, split into sub-missions,\n    or merged when scope overlaps. The lifecycle must accommodate these.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-lifecycle.flexiarg", :sha256 "78eee0c50b9af03f21a6225c21799b5c724ae873dfd95aee9724be5aac787001"}, :situation-source "Mission status fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The mission is in VERIFY with passed checks, a surfaced V-1 precondition, and named refinements."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Apply the mission state machine:\n\n    ```\n    :greenfield → :scoped → :active → :blocked → :review → :done\n                     ↑          ↓         ↓\n                     └──────────┴─────────┘ (can regress)\n    ```\n\n    State definitions:\n    - :greenfield - Idea captured, no work plan\n    - :scoped - Success criteria, boundaries, dependencies defined\n    - :active - Work in progress, owner assigned\n    - :blocked - Waiting on dependency (cite blocker)\n    - :review - Work complete, awaiting verification\n    - :done - Success criteria met, evidence recorded\n\n    Transition requirements:\n    - greenfield → scoped: Mission doc has success criteria + scope\n    - scoped → active: Owner assigned, dependencies clear\n    - active → blocked: Blocker cited with link to blocking mission\n    - active → review: All success criteria addressed\n    - review → done: Evidence verified by reviewer\n    - Any → :abandoned: Explicit decision with rationale\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/futon-theory/mission-lifecycle.flexiarg", :sha256 "78eee0c50b9af03f21a6225c21799b5c724ae873dfd95aee9724be5aac787001"}, :situation-source "Combined lifecycle pattern and status.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "An auditable VERIFY-stage mission with successes and remaining conditions distinguished."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/handoff-preserves-context", :source-sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3", :pattern-rationale "Explicit ownership identifies the parties responsible for preserving decisions and evidence across sessions.", :fragment-index 2, :sentence-id "s4", :fragment {:start 471, :end 494, :text "**Owner:** Joe + Claude", :intent "report", :target "mission ownership", :rationale "The field assigns joint responsibility for the mission."}, :roles ["context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/handoff-preserves-context", :objects {:G {:text "    Handoffs convert ephemeral session state into persistent project state. They enable distributed and asynchronous work without context collapse.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab exports session context to `lab/raw`, `lab/stubs`, and `lab/trace` (`dev/lab-export-claude.clj`), plus summaries via `fulab-summary` and `fulab-session-report`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Handoff pattern applied to joint ownership.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether decisions, verification findings, open preconditions, and next actions remain transferable between the named owners."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Continuity matters: the work is incremental, context is expensive to rebuild, or progress would be lost.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "agent/handoff-preserves-context THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Incremental work needs durable ownership, decisions, open questions, and evidence anchors."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Without explicit handoff, successors face cold starts: they repeat discoveries, miss constraints, or contradict prior decisions.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Mission owner field.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Joe and Claude jointly own War Machine Wiring."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Define a handoff record that captures: current state hypothesis, decisions made and why, open questions, scope boundaries, next actions, evidence/trail anchors, and any provisional-claim ledger. Emit it at session end or when transferring to another agent.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/handoff-preserves-context.flexiarg", :sha256 "403a43dfe0b4ae903c1e7ca249ffe8b43715b998b27262f75b3168028a0f3bb3"}, :situation-source "Combined handoff pattern and owner field.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A mission record either owner can continue without reconstructing prior reasoning."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :source-sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4", :pattern-rationale "The repository roles describe connected regions of the shared stack rather than isolated projects.", :fragment-index 3, :sentence-id "s5", :fragment {:start 495, :end 637, :text "**Repos:** futon5a (mission home), futon3c (head), futon3 (manifold + pair-mission), futon2 (AIF inspiration), futon5 (wiring-diagram pattern)", :intent "report", :target "cross-repository responsibility map", :rationale "The field assigns the mission home, control head, manifold, AIF reference, and diagram vocabulary to distinct repositories."}, :roles ["context" "dependency"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :objects {:G {:text "    ALFWorld taught us that text descriptions of rooms and objects naturally produce first-person inhabitation language. But the futon hypergraph has the same structure: nodes are locations (files, functions, missions), hyperedges are relationships (scholia, dependencies, presence), and traversal is navigation. \"I found the multiplex function in drawbridge/core.clj\" is phenomenologically identical to \"I found the vase on the dresser.\" The difference is that the hypergraph is real and mutable — agents can add nodes, create hyperedges, annotate each other's work. The game world writes itself.\n\n    + evidence: futon4 hyperedge model (arxana-store.el:565) — {:hx/type, :hx/endpoints [{:role/source, :role/target, :role/passage}]} — N-ary typed relations stored in XTDB.\n\n    + evidence: ALFWorld session (2026-02-13) — 2 games completed with first-person language (\"I found the vase\", \"I'm at the fridge\"). Same phenomenology emerged when exploring Drawbridge code (\"P-1 and P-6 are already implemented\").\n\n    + evidence: futon3 agency.mm — Mermaid diagram showing Agency topology. Describes one subgraph of the world; the full world is the union of all futon repos as a hypergraph.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern world model applied to the repository assignments.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether it connects these repository roles into one inspectable operating topology rather than treating them as isolated services."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You want agents to inhabit a rich, shared, mutable world where they can perceive objects, other agents, and the consequences of actions — rather than operating as isolated processes that happen to share a filesystem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The real world is the union of connected Futon repositories and their typed relationships."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The instinct is to build a game world as a separate layer: a dedicated server with game state, turn ordering, observation endpoints. This is how ALFWorld works (HTTP server wrapping TextWorld), and it produces a clean but isolated experience. The real work happens in the codebase, the database, the mission documents — but those feel like \"infrastructure\" rather than \"world.\" Agents treat them as APIs to query, not as places to be.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Mission repository map.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Five repositories supply the mission home, head, manifold, AIF reference, and diagram vocabulary."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Recognize that the futon stack IS the game world. futon1 (XTDB) is the persistent map. futon2 (ant hill) is the ecology. futon3 (Agency, Drawbridge, IRC, peripherals) is the coordination layer. futon4 (Arxana) is the hypertext fabric — hyperedges with typed roles connecting documents, code, annotations, and agents. futon5 (wiring diagrams) describes the world's structure. futon6 (math dictionary / proof engine) is a quest zone. The agents are already in the game; the task is making the game legible, not building a separate one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and repository map.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A cross-repository topology with explicit roles and navigable interfaces."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :pattern-rationale "The endpoint claim points to the exact mission artifact that defines the head.", :fragment-index 4, :sentence-id "s7", :fragment {:start 691, :end 762, :text "\n- `futon3c/holes/missions/M-war-machine.md` — the head: move-selection", :intent "report", :target "War Machine head endpoint", :rationale "The reference identifies the War Machine mission as the bridge's move-selection head."}, :roles ["dependency" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the head endpoint.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by checking head behavior and responsibility against the cited mission artifact."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Substantive claims require exact evidence anchors."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Head endpoint fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-war-machine.md is cited as the move-selection head."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and mission reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A bridge whose control-head claim is independently inspectable."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :source-sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363", :pattern-rationale "The listed control activities are the state-producing operations whose relationship to external obligations must remain visible.", :fragment-index 5, :sentence-id "s8", :fragment {:start 763, :end 821, :text "  policy, bidding, Tick/Click dispatch, recurring AIF tick", :intent "report", :target "War Machine head responsibilities", :rationale "The continuation enumerates the head's selection, bidding, dispatch, and recurring inference responsibilities."}, :roles ["action" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :objects {:G {:text "    The war machine can be captured by the institution it created. Without an explicit test, the stack quietly redirects nomadic practice toward self-reproduction.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "State-capture rule applied to head responsibilities.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether selection, bidding, dispatch, and recurrence remain bounded by explicit external obligations and observable outcomes."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Infrastructure maintenance begins to dominate the work mix and stack activity starts serving more stack activity than external deposition.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "war-machine/state-capture THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "War Machine activity must remain tied to outside obligations instead of quietly serving stack reproduction."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Head responsibilities fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The head performs policy selection, bidding, Tick/Click dispatch, and recurring AIF ticks."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and head responsibility list.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "An autonomous control loop whose activity is attributable to grounded obligations."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :pattern-rationale "The policy-tuning dependency is anchored to its exact mission file.", :fragment-index 6, :sentence-id "s9", :fragment {:start 822, :end 892, :text "- `futon3c/holes/missions/M-war-machine-tuning.md` — the head's policy", :intent "report", :target "War Machine policy-tuning endpoint", :rationale "The reference identifies the mission responsible for tuning the head's policy."}, :roles ["dependency" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the tuning endpoint.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by checking tuning assumptions and policy changes against the cited mission."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A responsibility claim must point to a source another observer can inspect."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Policy-tuning endpoint fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-war-machine-tuning.md is cited as the policy-tuning endpoint."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and mission reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A policy-tuning dependency with a concrete verification path."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :source-sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363", :pattern-rationale "A tuning surface affects how the War Machine allocates activity and therefore belongs in its inspectable control state.", :fragment-index 7, :sentence-id "s10", :fragment {:start 893, :end 909, :text "  tuning surface", :intent "report", :target "policy-tuning surface", :rationale "The continuation states that the referenced mission exposes the head's tuning surface."}, :roles ["context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :objects {:G {:text "    The war machine can be captured by the institution it created. Without an explicit test, the stack quietly redirects nomadic practice toward self-reproduction.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "State-capture constraint applied to policy tuning.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether tuning choices improve grounded obligation closure without increasing self-directed stack activity beyond its bound."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Infrastructure maintenance begins to dominate the work mix and stack activity starts serving more stack activity than external deposition.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "war-machine/state-capture THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Stack control surfaces need tests that expose whether activity supports external work."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Tuning-surface fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The tuning mission exposes the head's policy-tuning surface."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and tuning role.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A tuning surface that can distinguish useful policy adaptation from institutional capture."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :source-sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4", :pattern-rationale "The manifold is the legible shared-world representation to which War Machine state is being connected.", :fragment-index 8, :sentence-id "s11", :fragment {:start 910, :end 977, :text "- `futon3/holes/missions/M-live-geometric-stack.md` — the manifold:", :intent "report", :target "live geometric manifold endpoint", :rationale "The reference identifies the live geometric stack as the manifold side of the bridge."}, :roles ["dependency" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph", :objects {:G {:text "    ALFWorld taught us that text descriptions of rooms and objects naturally produce first-person inhabitation language. But the futon hypergraph has the same structure: nodes are locations (files, functions, missions), hyperedges are relationships (scholia, dependencies, presence), and traversal is navigation. \"I found the multiplex function in drawbridge/core.clj\" is phenomenologically identical to \"I found the vase on the dresser.\" The difference is that the hypergraph is real and mutable — agents can add nodes, create hyperedges, annotate each other's work. The game world writes itself.\n\n    + evidence: futon4 hyperedge model (arxana-store.el:565) — {:hx/type, :hx/endpoints [{:role/source, :role/target, :role/passage}]} — N-ary typed relations stored in XTDB.\n\n    + evidence: ALFWorld session (2026-02-13) — 2 games completed with first-person language (\"I found the vase\", \"I'm at the fridge\"). Same phenomenology emerged when exploring Drawbridge code (\"P-1 and P-6 are already implemented\").\n\n    + evidence: futon3 agency.mm — Mermaid diagram showing Agency topology. Describes one subgraph of the world; the full world is the union of all futon repos as a hypergraph.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Pattern shared-world rule applied to the manifold endpoint.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether War Machine state becomes a live, navigable part of the existing stack manifold."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    You want agents to inhabit a rich, shared, mutable world where they can perceive objects, other agents, and the consequences of actions — rather than operating as isolated processes that happen to share a filesystem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The stack's actual files, missions, and relations constitute the shared world."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The instinct is to build a game world as a separate layer: a dedicated server with game state, turn ordering, observation endpoints. This is how ALFWorld works (HTTP server wrapping TextWorld), and it produces a clean but isolated experience. The real work happens in the codebase, the database, the mission documents — but those feel like \"infrastructure\" rather than \"world.\" Agents treat them as APIs to query, not as places to be.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Manifold endpoint fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-live-geometric-stack is the manifold endpoint of the bridge."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Recognize that the futon stack IS the game world. futon1 (XTDB) is the persistent map. futon2 (ant hill) is the ecology. futon3 (Agency, Drawbridge, IRC, peripherals) is the coordination layer. futon4 (Arxana) is the hypertext fabric — hyperedges with typed roles connecting documents, code, annotations, and agents. futon5 (wiring diagrams) describes the world's structure. futon6 (math dictionary / proof engine) is a quest zone. The agents are already in the game; the task is making the game legible, not building a separate one.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/gauntlet/world-is-hypergraph.flexiarg", :sha256 "7a16f822bbdd129e3ebf2e2810663044d0d1fa29df1dc08c48865e031fd6c6d4"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and manifold reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A control head visibly embedded in the live geometric world."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :source-sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3", :pattern-rationale "Live geometric quantities need their rules and substrate observations attached so their values remain interpretable.", :fragment-index 9, :sentence-id "s12", :fragment {:start 978, :end 1032, :text "  live (T, ∇, Δ, drift) over the futon-stack substrate", :intent "report", :target "live geometric state variables", :rationale "The continuation names the live geometric quantities represented over the stack substrate."}, :roles ["context" "condition"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number", :objects {:G {:text "      Checkable disputes converge; unchecked ones escalate. A warrant\n      makes the number falsifiable at the step grain — which is what\n      separates evidence from assertion (kin: the evidence-over-\n      assertion discipline; [[measurement/error-needs-structure-to-teach]]\n      is this pattern applied to error records specifically).\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Measurement warrant applied to the live variables.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether every geometric quantity carries its computation, substrate inputs, window, and exclusions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      You record a computed metric that a decision will consume — or\n      that a person may later contest.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Computed quantities must carry rules, inputs, and assumptions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      The record carries only the value: the choice of rule, the input\n      window, and the exclusions live in code history and heads — so\n      when the number is disputed (and load-bearing numbers always\n      eventually are), the dispute becomes archaeology or authority\n      instead of arithmetic.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Live-state fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The manifold represents live T, ∇, Δ, and drift over the stack substrate."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Attach the warrant to the number where it is stored: the rule\n      (or its id/sha), the inputs (or pointers to them), and the\n      exclusions/assumptions. The test: a skeptical reader can\n      recompute the number from the record alone, or point at exactly\n      which warranted step they reject.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and state-variable description.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Recomputable live geometry whose changes can be challenged at the calculation step."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :pattern-rationale "The diagnostic dependency is anchored to a concrete mission artifact.", :fragment-index 10, :sentence-id "s13", :fragment {:start 1033, :end 1096, :text "- `futon3/holes/missions/M-pattern-application-diagnostic.md` —", :intent "report", :target "pattern-application diagnostic endpoint", :rationale "The reference identifies the pair mission responsible for diagnosing pattern applications."}, :roles ["dependency" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the diagnostic endpoint.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by checking pattern-application diagnoses against the cited mission and its evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Claims about diagnostic responsibility need concrete artifact anchors."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Diagnostic endpoint fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "M-pattern-application-diagnostic is cited as the relevant pair mission."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and mission reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A bridge whose diagnostic dependency is inspectable rather than inferred."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :source-sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f", :pattern-rationale "The interface connects stored mission material to an active graph in which new boundaries and relationships can be represented.", :fragment-index 11, :sentence-id "s14", :fragment {:start 1097, :end 1152, :text "  substrate-2's pair-mission, boundary-growth interface", :intent "report", :target "boundary-growth interface", :rationale "The continuation assigns the diagnostic mission the role of substrate-2 pair mission and boundary-growth interface."}, :roles ["dependency" "action"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph", :objects {:G {:text "      A unified, pattern-indexed graph enables reasoning/learning across boundaries while respecting each project's autonomy and\n      identity.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Activation pattern applied to the pair-mission interface.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by whether boundary growth integrates new pattern evidence into the active graph while preserving source identity."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "      Open mathematical repositories (\"deep storage\") already exist-PlanetMath, arXiv, nLab, wikis, code archives-holding\n      enormous value but lacking uniform structure and computational affordances.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Stored fragments gain utility when activated in a coherent, provenance-preserving graph."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "      Treating each repository as its own universe squanders synergies and makes it hard for humans or agents to form a unified\n      mental map of mathematics.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Boundary-growth fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The pair mission supplies substrate-2's boundary-growth interface."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Use HDM/FUTON6 as an aggregation + activation layer: ingest key fragments from deep storage into a coherent graph, annotate\n      them with patterns, proof skeletons, and cross-links, and maintain mappings back to origin sites for provenance.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hdm/deep-storage-to-active-graph.flexiarg", :sha256 "5394a281f2def43f04a7643e1ad809a528edf3dfaaa38712902cced71475557f"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and interface role.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A provenance-preserving interface from stored pattern records to live boundary growth."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :pattern-rationale "The mechanics claim points to the exact documentation artifact where it can be checked.", :fragment-index 12, :sentence-id "s16", :fragment {:start 1228, :end 1273, :text "\n- `futon2/doc/aif-engine.md` — AIF mechanics", :intent "report", :target "AIF mechanics reference", :rationale "The cross-reference names the document supplying the underlying AIF mechanics."}, :roles ["dependency" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the mechanics reference.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by checking its AIF operations against the cited mechanics document."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Mechanism claims require a file, trace, test, or quotation."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "AIF mechanics fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "aif-engine.md is cited as the source for AIF mechanics."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and document reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A wiring policy whose AIF mechanics have an explicit audit source."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :pattern-rationale "The implementation claim is paired with concrete source and test locations.", :fragment-index 13, :sentence-id "s17", :fragment {:start 1274, :end 1346, :text "- `futon2/src/ants/clj_ants_aif.clj` (+ tests under `futon2/test/ants/`)", :intent "report", :target "tested AIF ants implementation", :rationale "The reference identifies both the implementation and the directory containing its tests."}, :roles ["dependency" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the code and test anchors.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by reproducing relevant behavior through the named implementation and tests."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Implementation claims should expose source and test evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "AIF ants implementation fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "clj_ants_aif.clj and its tests are cited as the AIF ants implementation."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and implementation reference.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A tested implementation precedent for autonomous AIF behavior."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :source-sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363", :pattern-rationale "The foraging precedent offers a concrete comparison for whether autonomous stack activity remains connected to external obligations.", :fragment-index 14, :sentence-id "s18", :fragment {:start 1347, :end 1409, :text "  — AIF ants implementation, the autonomous-foraging reference", :intent "report", :target "autonomous-foraging implementation precedent", :rationale "The continuation designates the AIF ants implementation as the autonomous-foraging reference for this mission."}, :roles ["dependency" "rationale"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :objects {:G {:text "    The war machine can be captured by the institution it created. Without an explicit test, the stack quietly redirects nomadic practice toward self-reproduction.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "State-capture constraints applied to the foraging precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by comparing its autonomous search policy with the reference while requiring every selected action to identify an outside obligation."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Infrastructure maintenance begins to dominate the work mix and stack activity starts serving more stack activity than external deposition.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "war-machine/state-capture THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Autonomy needs explicit checks against self-maintenance displacing external obligations."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Autonomous-foraging fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The AIF ants implementation is the autonomous-foraging reference."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and implementation precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Autonomous foraging constrained by observable external-purpose checks."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :pattern-rationale "The head-specific framing claim is tied to named mission documents.", :fragment-index 15, :sentence-id "s19", :fragment {:start 1410, :end 1476, :text "- `futon2/holes/M-aif-head.md`, `M-aif4iad.md` — head-specific AIF", :intent "report", :target "head-specific AIF references", :rationale "The line identifies two mission documents containing AIF formulations specific to the control head."}, :roles ["dependency" "context"], :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the paired references.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by testing its head interpretation against both cited framing documents."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "agent/evidence-over-assertion THEN.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Conceptual framing claims need exact source anchors."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {: