war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "war-machine/state-capture THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Autonomy needs explicit checks against self-maintenance displacing external obligations."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Autonomous-foraging fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The AIF ants implementation is the autonomous-foraging reference."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and implementation precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Autonomous foraging constrained by observable external-purpose checks."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 15], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"agent/evidence-over-assertion\" 15]", :span {:start 1410, :end 1476}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9