ate-capture", :objects {:G {:text "    The war machine can be captured by the institution it created. Without an explicit test, the stack quietly redirects nomadic practice toward self-reproduction.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "State-capture constraints applied to the foraging precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by comparing its autonomous search policy with the reference while requiring every selected action to identify an outside obligation."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Infrastructure maintenance begins to dominate the work mix and stack activity starts serving more stack activity than external deposition.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "war-machine/state-capture THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Autonomy needs explicit checks against self-maintenance displacing external obligations."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Autonomous-foraging fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The AIF ants implementation is the autonomous-foraging reference."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and implementation precedent.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Autonomous foraging constrained by observable external-purpose checks."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 15], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-war-machine-wiring/M-war-machine-wiring/policy-2629917c87a61978be8f/[\"agent/evidence-over-assertion\" 15]", :span {:start 1410, :end 1476}, :source-text-digest "bd0f29407a1be7c77a6fb41f33fff97b01e22e9a0b093b4ee693af0197ba9ed4", :analysis-digest "c8402106cd699388b85a9387c851b2a45fd28e0cdf6445524f21fc236efa72a7", :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :square-digest "c66485872e08465c724471507f954fbcd51fb8f574edc40e9aaa2fdc0bb644e5"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Evidence rule applied to the paired references.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Evaluate a complete cascade by testing its head interpretation against both cited framing documents."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, hum