w, and the exclusions live in code history and heads — so\n      when the number is disputed (and load-bearing numbers always\n      eventually are), the dispute becomes archaeology or authority\n      instead of arithmetic.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Projection-axes fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The piano-roll trace is projected over substrate and time."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "      Attach the warrant to the number where it is stored: the rule\n      (or its id/sha), the inputs (or pointers to them), and the\n      exclusions/assumptions. The test: a skeptical reader can\n      recompute the number from the record alone, or point at exactly\n      which warranted step they reject.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number.flexiarg", :sha256 "415a41bc2fc385ebc02e7cae2dc20d0b484790afa9b14a7958fc66853652e7e3"}, :situation-source "Combined pattern and projection axes.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "A recomputable substrate-by-time trace whose plotted values remain contestable."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [24], :pattern "measurement/warrant-travels-with-the-number"} {:pattern-rationale "The prototype claim supplies exact implementation and rendered-output anchors.", :fragment-span {:start 1894, :end 1962}, :occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 25], :roles ["dependency" "context"], :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :sentence-id "s29", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative tr