onstraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "Cross-reference constrained by external-obligation checks.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Use Mission Control as grounded input, not self-maintenance evidence."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["war-machine/state-capture" 6], :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :roles ["context" "condition"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"war-machine/state-capture\" 6]", :span {:start 445, :end 489}, :source-text-digest "9c2f467e8d5062961da62bae3a5d3b2b064f048a9354e7be0bfd5dfc025d2aad", :analysis-digest "e183844e1fd2569431413d615fb7b997a8182cdd0b86f14175ed3b83e21e5e4d", :source-sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363", :square-digest "b2d629045086b97f206ff48d92debabb1835e22edb7fdcc251e51cef7b3ba4a4"}, :square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "war-machine/state-capture", :objects {:G {:text "    The war machine can be captured by the institution it created. Without an explicit test, the stack quietly redirects nomadic practice toward self-reproduction.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "State-capture rule and recorded portfolio scope.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "The active portfolio grounds the geometry’s state."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Infrastructure maintenance begins to dominate the work mix and stack activity starts serving more stack activity than external deposition.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg THEN/BECAUSE.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "Infrastructure should expose the outside work it supports."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Some self-maintenance is necessary, and there is a live philosophical question about which side is the nomad and which is the State. The pattern matters when self-maintenance dominates instead of supporting grounded obligations.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "M-stack-geometry.md observation-scope fragment.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Mission Control observes about 25 active missions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Use pocketwatch-style constraints and explicit external-sorry checks: every stack work item must answer which outside obligation it closes, and stack hours must stay bounded relative to portfolio and consulting hours.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/war-machine/state-capture.flexiarg", :sha256 "b45598fb80725dfb4b7deadf520355feaca633dc9d1238c037c7fad654b6d363"}, :situation-source "~25-mission scope interpreted through state-capture.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Use active missions as the grounding population for geometry."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}} {:occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 7], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :roles ["dependency" "context"], :fragment-indices [], :origin :selected, :provenance {:reading-record-id "M-stack-geometry/M-stack-geometry/policy-c7d7518e1e185c2e2318/[\"agent/evidence-over-assertion\" 7]", :span {:start 518, :end 542}